+### 4.3 list_sessions
+
+Asks for the conversation list of the user the connection was authenticated as; the server answers with a `session_list` message (§ 5.9) and never sends one unsolicited. There is no field by which a frame may name another user: a `userId` a client sends is ignored, because the user id is taken from the connection and never from the frame ([validated by: answers list_sessions for the authenticated user with ISO dates, forwarding limit and before while ignoring any client userId](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L60), [validated by: answers list_sessions with the socket user's own conversations as ISO dates, however the frame names its user](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L94)).
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "list_sessions",
+  "limit": 10,
+  "before": { "updatedAt": "2026-01-01T00:05:00.000Z", "sessionId": "s3" }
+}
+```
+
+| Field               | Type             | Required | Description                                                              |
+| ------------------- | ---------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
+| `type`              | string           | Yes      | `"list_sessions"`                                                        |
+| `limit`             | number           | No       | Maximum rows to return, a non-negative integer                            |
+| `before`            | object           | No       | Page cursor: the last row the client saw                                  |
+| `before.updatedAt`  | string \| number | No       | The cursor row's activity time, an ISO-8601 string or epoch milliseconds  |
+| `before.sessionId`  | string           | No       | The cursor row's session id, 1–128 characters                             |
+
+Constraints:
+
+- `limit`, when present, MUST be a non-negative integer, and `before`, when present, MUST carry both halves, since a cursor of one half alone would drop a conversation tied on activity time. Violation of either constraint results in an `error` response with code `INVALID_MESSAGE`, and the session store is not asked ([validated by: accepts a bare list_sessions frame and one with a limit and cursor, and rejects a malformed limit or before naming the field](../../src/transport/ws/validation.test.ts#L24), [validated by: accepts a bare list_sessions frame and rejects a malformed limit or before with INVALID_MESSAGE without calling listFor](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L130)).
+- A history request is not a turn: it is answered off the per-session lock, so a `list_sessions` sent while a turn is running is answered before that turn's `stream_end` ([validated by: answers a list_sessions at once while a run is pending, before that turn has sent its stream_end](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L745)).
+- Picking a conversation from the list needs no new frame: the client reconnects with `?sessionId=<id>`, whose ownership check and replay the resume behaviour of Section 2.3 already provides.
